upstream: https://github.com/glfw/glfw
tag:      3.4
sha256:   c038d34200234d071fae9345bc455e4a8f2f544ab60150765d7704e08f3dac01  (3.4.tar.gz)

trimmed to the library build inputs only: include/GLFW public headers, src/
(all .c/.m/.h, including the pre-generated mappings.h), deps/wayland protocol
XML, and LICENSE.md. upstream CMake files, docs, tests, examples, and the
example-only deps/ entries are not carried.

patched with the upstream IME support work, which no GLFW release carries yet
(3.5.1 does not; it is still open against master):

  pull:    https://github.com/glfw/glfw/pull/2130 ("Add IME support for each platform")
  branch:  https://github.com/clear-code/glfw/tree/im-support
  head:    068858eece20cd6b6128f6f07a1d61f2dc2cbfaf ("Wayland: Fix text input v3 preedit cursor offsets")
  base:    92dcf4ce74f2e2554a98fea09be7c705c17daa5a (glfw master, the branch's merge base)

taken: `git diff 92dcf4ce 068858ee -- include src deps`, every hunk except
src/CMakeLists.txt, applied to the 3.4 tree. that adds
deps/wayland/text-input-unstable-v1.xml and text-input-unstable-v3.xml, which
tools/build-glfw.sh runs through wayland-scanner. master is 113 commits past
3.4, so six files needed resolving against 3.4:

  include/GLFW/glfw3.h  GLFW_IME keeps upstream's value 0x00033007. master's
                        GLFW_UNLIMITED_MOUSE_BUTTONS (3.5) is not taken, nor
                        its mention in the glfwSetInputMode docs.
  src/init.c            onTheSpotIMStyle defaults to GLFW_FALSE (3.4 keeps
  src/internal.h        GLFWbool where master uses bool). master's
                        disableMouseButtonLimit window field is not taken.
  src/input.c           only the GLFW_IME input mode cases are taken.
  src/win32_init.c      imm32 is freed in 3.4's freeLibraries().
  src/wl_window.c       pointerHandleButton keeps 3.4's pointerFocus/hovered
                        handling and activates text-input v1 on any press, as
                        upstream does.

one local fix sits on top, not yet upstream: on wayland, the patch's
text-input v3 done handler re-commits the cursor rectangle, and a compositor
that answers every commit with a done event (kwin does) loops forever, firing
the preedit callback tens of thousands of times a second. the rectangle is now
committed only when it differs from the one last committed since enable.

patches/ime-support.patch is the adapted upstream diff against the 3.4 tree and
patches/wayland-text-input-v3-commit-loop.patch is the local fix, paths
relative to this directory. on a fresh 3.4 extract,
`patch -p1 < patches/ime-support.patch` then
`patch -p1 < patches/wayland-text-input-v3-commit-loop.patch` reproduce the
vendored sources exactly.

to bump: re-extract the new tag and copy the same four paths. if the new tag
carries IME support, drop the patches whose change it already has; otherwise
re-apply the newest im-support head, and the local fix while upstream lacks
it, and record both here. see tools/build-glfw.sh for the compilation matrix
that consumes them.
